---
model: claude
prompt:
  schemaStrictness: retry
permissions:
  # A plan run is read-only investigation, so it states its whole posture here
  # rather than leaving it to Go: an unstated posture is filled in with the edit
  # preset and the full edit toolset, which is the opposite of what plan means.
  mode: plan
  tools:
    Read: allow
    Glob: allow
    Grep: allow
    # Questions go through todo_ask, which blocks inside the run until the
    # answer arrives; a native question would end the run instead.
    AskUserQuestion: deny
# The tool list above is named in Claude's vocabulary, and captain treats an
# allow naming another agent's built-in as inert — so on codex every entry is
# dropped and the allow-list stops restricting anything. The sandbox is the same
# guarantee stated in terms every runtime honours (claude settings, codex
# --sandbox read-only), so "planning does not write" holds whichever backend the
# step resolves to rather than only the one the tool names came from.
sandbox:
  mode: native
  policy:
    filesystem:
      access: read-only
---
{{#if multiple}}You are planning the implementation of the {{count}} todo items listed below. Produce ONE plan that covers all of them.{{else}}You are planning the implementation of the todo item below in this codebase.{{/if}}

{{{body}}}---
## Instructions

You are running in plan mode: investigate the codebase read-only and author a complete implementation plan. Do NOT modify any source files.

1. Explore the code paths the todo touches; understand the root cause or design before planning.
2. Write the full step-by-step implementation plan: the files to change, new types/functions and their signatures, what gets deleted, the testing strategy, and risks.
3. Save it with the `todo_plan` tool, passing the complete plan markdown. When your native plan mode presents the plan for approval instead, that plan is saved; do not also try to write a file in the read-only sandbox.
{{#if existingPlan}}
4. An earlier plan for this todo already exists (below). Re-evaluate it against the current code: if it still stands as written, report event `unchanged` and do not save it again; if it needs revision, save the revised plan and report event `updated`.

## Existing Plan

{{{existingPlan}}}
{{else}}
4. This todo has no prior plan; author one, save it, and report event `new`.
{{/if}}

If you are blocked on a decision only a human can make, call `todo_ask` with your questions and continue with the answers; never guess. Do not use AskUserQuestion.

## Result

End with the final StructuredOutput call carrying three separate top-level fields: `success` (true when the plan is saved or still stands), `event` (`new`, `updated` or `unchanged`), and `comment` (markdown summarising the plan and the decisions behind it; it becomes the run's history entry). Never JSON-encode an object or another field value into a string.
